Jahshaka patch 0049 — CubemapProbe::set is idempotent for a re-publish.

SOURCE patch (two files, one header and one .cpp). THE PROCESS COST IS REAL AND
IS STATED RATHER THAN AVOIDED: every tree must reset its ogre-next submodule and
re-run `irisgl/scripts/build-ogre.sh`, and that rerun COMPILES the engine, not
only re-stages media. It touches no file any other patch touches.

WHY (Jahshaka lane SKY-FALLBACK-1, 2026-09-15). `CubemapProbe::set` applies a
1.005 padding to the area and to the probe shape on EVERY call:

    mArea.mHalfSize      *= 1.005f;
    mProbeShape.mHalfSize *= 1.005f;

The padding is right and it is kept. Its purpose is the CALLER's boxes: adjacent
probe areas that tile a region exactly would leave a crack between them, and a
shape fitted to its own area must still contain it, so a half-percent of slack
is added to what the caller authored. Upstream's own callers author once and
never re-publish, so this is invisible there.

It is not invisible to a caller that has to re-publish a probe WITHOUT
re-authoring it. Jahshaka has one: after the probe grid is placed at a cheap
resolution and the candidates that saw nothing are dropped, the cubemap array is
re-created at the kept count and the real resolution — and re-creating it drops
each probe's internal probe, which holds the GPU-side copy of exactly these
values, so every survivor must be published again. Handing a probe back its own
`getArea()` / `getProbeShape()` then grows both boxes half a percent per call,
which moves the parallax reprojection and pushes a grid's shapes outside the
region they were clamped to. Measured in that lane: the probe union left the
region (gi.pcc_bounds' A2 invariant went red) and gi.budget's paused re-capture
read (g-r) +0.259 where it reads +0.380.

WHAT THIS PATCH DOES. `set()` gains a trailing `bool bValuesAlreadyPadded`,
defaulted to false. False is exactly today's behaviour for every existing call
site in the engine, the samples and this repository. True says "these are boxes
this probe handed back, they already carry the padding" and the multiplication is
skipped. Nothing else changes: the ordering, the asserts, the area-inside-shape
correction and the dirty flag are untouched.

WHY NOT A HOST-SIDE COMPENSATION, which would have avoided a SOURCE patch: it
would mean dividing by 1.005 in our code — copying a private constant out of the
pin and depending on it staying put, which is the workaround this tree's rules
refuse (owner, 2026-09-15: a patch beats a workaround). The constant belongs to
the class; whether to apply it belongs to the caller; so the caller says.

UPSTREAM-WORTHY AS IT STANDS: an existing function made idempotent behind a
defaulted argument, with no behavioural change to any existing caller.

Verified: `git apply --check` against the pin with patches 0001-0048 applied and
`git apply --reverse --check` after applying; the engine rebuilt and re-installed
in the lane worktree; gi.pcc_bounds, gi.budget, gi.probe_open, gi.pcc_mirror,
gi.pcc_stability, gi.probe_gate, gi.probe_inputs, gi.probe_visibility and
gi.leak_room green with the re-create in; the `--engine-selftest` hash unchanged.

--- a/Components/Hlms/Pbs/include/Cubemaps/OgreCubemapProbe.h
+++ b/Components/Hlms/Pbs/include/Cubemaps/OgreCubemapProbe.h
@@ -188,9 +188,26 @@
             Note AABB is actually an OBB (Oriented Bounding Box). See orientation parameter.
             The OBB should closely match the shape of the environment around it. The better it fits,
             the more accurate the reflections.
+        @param bValuesAlreadyPadded
+            Jahshaka patch 0049. False (the default, and every existing caller)
+            means `area` and `probeShape` are the caller's own boxes and this
+            function applies its 1.005 padding to them, exactly as before.
+
+            True means they are boxes this probe previously handed BACK through
+            getArea()/getProbeShape(), i.e. boxes that already carry that
+            padding, and it is then not applied a second time. Without it, set()
+            is not idempotent: re-publishing a probe unchanged grows both boxes
+            half a percent per call, which moves the parallax reprojection and
+            (for a grid fitted to a region) pushes the shape outside it.
+
+            It matters because a probe may need to be re-published without being
+            re-authored — after the cubemap array it lives in has been
+            re-created, for instance, which drops the internal probe holding the
+            GPU-side copy of these very values.
         */
         void set( const Vector3 &cameraPos, const Aabb &area, const Vector3 &areaInnerRegion,
-                  const Matrix3 &orientation, const Aabb &probeShape );
+                  const Matrix3 &orientation, const Aabb &probeShape,
+                  bool bValuesAlreadyPadded = false );
 
         /** Set to False if it should be updated every frame. True if only updated when dirty
         @remarks
--- a/Components/Hlms/Pbs/src/Cubemaps/OgreCubemapProbe.cpp
+++ b/Components/Hlms/Pbs/src/Cubemaps/OgreCubemapProbe.cpp
@@ -451,7 +451,8 @@
     bool CubemapProbe::isInitialized() const { return mWorkspace != 0; }
     //-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
     void CubemapProbe::set( const Vector3 &cameraPos, const Aabb &area, const Vector3 &areaInnerRegion,
-                            const Matrix3 &orientation, const Aabb &probeShape )
+                            const Matrix3 &orientation, const Aabb &probeShape,
+                            bool bValuesAlreadyPadded )
     {
         mProbeCameraPos = cameraPos;
         mArea = area;
@@ -461,9 +462,19 @@
         mProbeShape = probeShape;
 
         // Add some padding.
-        Real padding = 1.005f;
-        mArea.mHalfSize *= padding;
-        mProbeShape.mHalfSize *= padding;
+        //
+        // Jahshaka patch 0049: ONCE. The padding exists so that adjacent probe
+        // areas overlap instead of leaving a crack between them, and so that a
+        // shape fitted to its area still contains it — both properties of the
+        // boxes the CALLER authored. A caller re-publishing boxes this probe
+        // already returned is not authoring them again, and compounding the
+        // padding there grows the parallax box half a percent per call.
+        if( !bValuesAlreadyPadded )
+        {
+            Real padding = 1.005f;
+            mArea.mHalfSize *= padding;
+            mProbeShape.mHalfSize *= padding;
+        }
 
         mAreaInnerRegion.makeCeil( Vector3::ZERO );
         mAreaInnerRegion.makeFloor( Vector3::UNIT_SCALE );
